      "excerpt": "Let E_K be the finite-dimensional rational module of polynomial maps $operatorname{End}(V)\tooperatorname{End}(V^{otimes d})$ of degree at most K, for KgedegPhi, with action $(gcdotPsi)(Y)=g^{otimes d}Psi(g^{-1}Yg)(g^{-1})^{otimes d}$. ... Weyl's theorem [F3] applied to the semisimple Lie algebra $mathfrak{sl}(V)$ gives an $mathfrak{sl}(V)$-stable complement to I_K. This complement is stable under $mathrm{SL}(V)$, since elementary matrices $exp(tE_{ij})$ generate that group ... together with scalar matrices they generate $mathrm{GL}(V)$ over $mathbb C$.",
